        "PMC10707036::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial CrMnFeCoNi bond coat has moderate toughness.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed CrMnFeCoNi bond coat is deposited on a Ni-based superalloy substrate.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 4 wt% ZrC can be introduced into CrMnFeCoNi HEA coatings by plasma transferred arc processing.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10707036::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thermal spraying is a suitable route for introducing approximately 4 wt% ZrC into this HEA bond coat.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Optimized particle size and spray dynamics will produce a uniform ZrC dispersion.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "ZrC mainly remains as a second phase in CrMnFeCoNi HEA coatings while having little influence on the main crystal structure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10707036::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The added ZrC particles will be uniformly dispersed and fine.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "During high-temperature exposure, ZrC will transform and segregate to form a coherent, stable ZrO2-rich sublayer at the bond-coat/TGO interface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "ZrC particles refine the CrMnFeCoNi coating microstructure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "ZrC particles act as nucleation sites during high-temperature exposure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr migrates to the oxidation front during high-temperature exposure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A ZrO2-rich sublayer limits oxygen ingress and outward metal diffusion through the bond coat.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Limiting oxygen ingress and metal outward diffusion reduces TGO growth stress and delays cracking and spallation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to untreated CrMnFeCoNi bond coats, the ZrC-modified coatings will exhibit thinner and more uniform TGO, slower oxidation, and better oxide adherence.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted oxidation improvements will enhance thermal-barrier-coating durability and reliability.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Untreated CrMnFeCoNi bond coats typically develop a non-uniform, thicker TGO and are more susceptible to oxidation-induced spallation.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The benefits should persist during oxidation and thermal cycling at about 1100°C for approximately 1000 hours when ZrC dispersion is optimized.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Non-uniform dispersion or excessive ceramic-phase formation could negate the predicted benefits.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Poorly controlled ZrC dispersion may cause brittle intermetallic phases that compromise mechanical integrity.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
  ],
